// A road with a dip and a fenced ember, the seed in an ember's pit, a wide pillar with a wall on its far side, a ladder beside a rising ember; the bloom is cut by the wall and becomes the mesa to the high road.
name Origin
rule B1234/S012345678
steps 4
hint The seed lies in the pit where an ember paces. The stone stands somewhere on the pillar's top, against the wall. The ladder climbs past a rising ember. Plant, come back down the ladder, Grow, then climb the bloom over the wall to the high road.
tip Four generations reach four cells out. The wall cut this bloom: count four back from its open edge and you have the stone. Wait on the ladder, at least five cells from it, before you grow.
intro The highest stone in the deepest cave. You have found where every ruin began. This is where you began: a seed in a pit, a stone on a pillar against a wall, and an ember rising and falling between them.
outro The last bloom grew from the highest point, and you climbed it into the light. You were its seed.
